    "body": "## Description\n\nMigrates `services/v2-api` off ad-hoc env handling (scattered `process.env.X` reads) onto the shared `env-shared` Config ABC, and wires up `pnpm generate:env` so a local `.env` is generated from AWS Parameter Store + inlined defaults instead of hand-maintained. Part of the BE-1709 effort to roll `generate:env` out across `services/`.\n\nType of change: refactor / infra\n\n## Changes Made\n\n- **New `src/utils/env.ts`** declaring the full reached env surface as a typed `Config`, composed from shared groups (`...GROUPS.base()`, `...GROUPS.temporal({ exclude: ['TEMPORAL_NAMESPACE'] })`, `...GROUPS.docsAuth()`, `...GROUPS.auth0()`, `...GROUPS.hasura()`), shared infra shorthand fields, and v2-api-specific fields (received-email idempotency cache, temporal connection-cache toggle, default Slack channel, notifications, n8n).\n- `WORKOS_API_KEY` is declared inline as `.storedConfig('v2-api/workos-api-key').secret()` (per-service secret, matching dashboard-api's convention), not a shared group. `RBAC_PROJECTION_QUEUE_URL` and `SOLA_ADMIN_API_KEY` use the canonical shared fields.\n- Converted all 11 of v2-api's own `process.env.X` reads to typed `env.X` (sola.ts, both workflows controllers, the received-email idempotency cache, temporal files). Left the infra-level `DEPLOYED_STAGE` reads as `process.env`.\n- Added a `generate:env` script; pointed `start` / `start:ts-node` / `nodemon` at the generated `.env`.\n- Added `env-shared` as a dependency.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `typecheck` + `lint` + `build` (tsoa codegen + tsc) all pass.\n- `pnpm -F v2-api generate:env` writes a complete 26-entry `.env` from dev Parameter Store (incl. decrypted `TEMPORAL_API_KEY`, `WORKOS_API_KEY`, `SOLA_ADMIN_API_KEY`, `DOCS_AUTH_PASSWORD`).\n- Config-load smoke: every field parses against the generated `.env` with **zero Zod errors**.\n- **Real boot** under Node 24 (`node build/server.js` with the generated `.env`): `Express server started on port: 5559`, `GET /swagger.json` → 200, clean log.\n- Helm cross-check: every `.storedConfig`/`.localDefault` field is set by helm in dev and prod — no gaps.\n\n## Rollout Plan\n\n- **Dev** Parameter Store keys are seeded: `sentry/dsn-v2-api`, `browser-contexts-bucket`, `browser-contexts-metadata-table`, `api-key-data-table`, and `v2-api/workos-api-key` (new this PR; value copied from the existing dev WorkOS key). `sola/admin-api-key` already existed.\n- **Production** Parameter Store entries are NOT yet populated — a separate step (`config add-parameter` with prod values) before any prod deploy that relies on `generate:env`. This PR does not change cluster behavior; helm still supplies these env vars in every cluster.\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n- `FILE_METADATA_TABLE` (read by authorization-shared) and `VARIABLE_DATA_TABLE` (set in v2-api helm) were confirmed out of scope — the former is unreachable on v2-api's code path, the latter has no reader in v2-api (likely stale chart copy).\n\n## Links\n\n- Linear ticket: [BE-1709](https://linear.app/sola-ai/issue/BE-1709/migrate-remaining-services) (parent BE-1706)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Refactor touches execution queuing, Temporal, Redis idempotency, and many secrets/infra vars, but deployed clusters still get env from helm; main risk is local/dev misconfiguration if `generate:env` is not run or Parameter Store is incomplete.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> **v2-api** moves from hand-maintained `.env.local` / scattered `process.env` reads to a typed **`env-shared` `Config`** in `src/utils/env.ts`, with local env produced by **`pnpm generate:env`** (Parameter Store + defaults) into **`.env`**.\n> \n> Runtime code now uses **`env.*`** for workflow/S3/Dynamo settings, Redis, Temporal API key and connection-cache toggle, and received-email idempotency cache options. **`SolaService`** drops per-field constructor throws in favor of schema-level validation. Local Temporal client wiring builds the address from **`env.TEMPORAL_ADDRESS`** and **`env.TEMPORAL_PORT`**. The idempotency cache factory always uses the configured enum (no invalid-type fallback log).\n> \n> **`start`**, **`start:ts-node`**, and **nodemon** source **`.env`** instead of **`.env.local`**; committed **`.env.local`** templates are removed. **`DEPLOYED_STAGE`** (and a few express-shared reads) stay on **`process.env`**.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 0c114da31ba59ae612daaf7ff59c4cd41748dce2. Bugbot is set up for automated code reviews on this repo. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->",
